@@ -153,6 +153,13 @@ Global sysctls
   exact same-kernel Tier2-without-WSS ablation; Tier2 then uses its original
   fixed demote watermark.  .. lzx-note
 
+  The two-generation filter controls entry into ``RELAX`` and ``STRENGTHEN``.
+  ``memory.tier2_stats`` reports that accepted value as
+  ``workingset_policy_action`` and the current live-headroom result as
+  ``workingset_action``.  The live result exits an exceptional action
+  immediately when its condition disappears, so a recovered cgroup does not
+  continue reclaiming until the next user-space event.  .. lzx-note
+
 Cgroup v2 files
 ===============
 
@@ -178,7 +185,7 @@ Each non-root memory cgroup has these files:
   Configuration, live values, EWMA, predicted time and per-cgroup counters.
   WSS builds also expose the effective headroom/usage watermark, predicted
   working set/resident/growth, raw and hysteresis-filtered action, confidence,
-  skips, fallbacks and hard-line overrides.  .. lzx-note
+  skips, fallbacks, hard-line overrides and live-action restores.  .. lzx-note
 
